<statement>
<p>
	This program returns an AI move to an available space in a Tic-Tac-Toe game based on your chosen strategy.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object containing the state of the current tic-tac-toe game.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>selection</pf> (1 x 1) integer — The absolute index of the chosen space.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Your grade on this program will be based on how well it does when it competes against the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>HW5P1_better_ai_move</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>code.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>I will simulate 1000 games against your code and the</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>TTT_ai_move_2</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>strategy. In half of the games, your code will have the first move.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Do not look up strategies online or ask anyone for help. This should be 100% your own AI strategy for Tic-Tac-Toe.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
